## 1. Introduction

This document outlines the technical specifications for the policies and procedures governing underwriting, claims management, risk assessment, and actuarial functions at Global Shield Insurance Company. These policies are crucial for ensuring compliance with legal regulations, maintaining operational efficiency, and enhancing customer satisfaction.

## 2. Policies Overview

### 2.1 Underwriting Policy

**Objective:** To establish guidelines for assessing risk and determining eligibility for insurance coverage.

**Key Components:**
- **Eligibility Criteria:** Applicants must provide a completed application form (Form U1) and any supporting documentation by the underwriting deadline of 30 days from application submission.
- **Risk Classification:** Risks will be classified into four categories: Low, Moderate, High, and Very High. Classification will be based on factors such as age, health status, and claims history.
- **Underwriting Decisions:** Underwriting decisions will be made by the Underwriting Committee, led by Sarah L. Williams (Head Underwriter), who will review applications weekly.
  
### 2.2 Claims Policy

**Objective:** To provide a structured approach for processing claims efficiently and fairly.

**Key Components:**
- **Claims Submission:** Claims must be submitted via the Claims Management System (CMS) within 60 days of the incident date.
- **Claims Review Process:** Claims will be reviewed within 15 business days by a Claims Adjuster, with oversight from Richard K. Adams (Claims Manager).
- **Dispute Resolution:** Disputes regarding claims decisions will be addressed by the Claims Review Board, which includes legal representation from Francesca B. Lee (Legal Counsel).

### 2.3 Risk Assessment Policy

**Objective:** To evaluate potential risks associated with insuring applicants and existing policyholders.

**Key Components:**
- **Risk Assessment Procedures:** Utilization of the Risk Assessment Tool (RAT) for quantitative analysis of applicant data.
- **Risk Mitigation Strategies:** Implementation of risk reduction measures for high-risk categories, including higher premiums or additional underwriting criteria.
- **Annual Risk Review:** Conducted by the Risk Management Team led by Thomas E. Reed (Chief Risk Officer) every January.

### 2.4 Actuarial Policy

**Objective:** To ensure accurate pricing of insurance products and reserve allocation.

**Key Components:**
- **Data Analysis:** The Actuarial Analysis System (AAS) will be used for statistical analysis of claims data and premium calculations.
- **Profitability Metrics:** Key performance indicators (KPIs) will be established, including loss ratios and expense ratios, analyzed quarterly by the actuary team led by Laura M. Chen (Lead Actuary).
- **Regulatory Compliance:** Adherence to the National Association of Insurance Commissioners (NAIC) requirements for financial reporting.

